===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*dus-|*dwi-|*steh₂-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|distance}}, {{m|enm|distaunce}}, {{m|enm|destance|t=disagreement, dispute; discrimination; armed conflict; hostility; trouble; space between two points; time interval}},<ref>{{R:MED Online|entry=distaunce|pos=n|id=MED12119}}</ref> from {{der|en|xno|distance}}, {{m|xno|distaunce}}, {{m|xno|destance}}, {{der|en|frm|distance}}, and {{der|en|fro|destance}}, {{m|fro|destaunce}}, {{m|fro|distaunce|t=debate; difference, distinction; discord, quarrel; dispute; space between two points; time interval}} (modern {{cog|fr|distance}}), and directly from their {{glossary|etymon}} {{der|en|la|distantia|t=difference, diversity; distance, remoteness; space between two points}} (whence also {{cog|LL.|distantia|t=disagreement; discrepancy; gap, opening; time interval}}), from {{m|la|distāns|t=being distant; standing apart}} + {{m|la|-ia|pos={{glossary|suffix}} forming {{glossary|feminine}} {{glossary|abstract noun}}s}}.<ref>{{R:OED Online|pos=n|id=8508487382|date=March 2024|nodot=1}}; {{R:Lexico|pos=n}}</ref> {{m|la||Distāns}} is the {{glossary|present}} {{glossary|active}} {{glossary|participle}} of {{m|la|distō|t=to be distant; to stand apart; to differ}}, from {{m|la|dis-|pos={{glossary|prefix}} meaning ‘apart, asunder; in two’}} + {{m|la|stō|t=to stand}} (ultimately from {{der|en|ine-pro|*steh₂-|t=to stand (up)}}).

The {{glossary|verb}} is derived from the noun.<ref>{{R:OED Online|pos=v|id=1975986022|date=July 2023|nodot=1}}; {{R:Lexico|pos=v}}</ref>

